From: PhantoNull <65261018+PhantoNull@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Configure: keep date diagnostics out of config.sh

Buildroot's reproducible date wrapper writes its SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH warning
to stderr and the timestamp to stdout. Capturing both into cf_time inserts
an uncommented second line beneath the generated configuration-time comment;
sourcing config.sh then tries to execute the weekday as a command.

Capture only the timestamp. Leave stderr connected to the build diagnostic
stream rather than globally hiding the wrapper warning.

Upstream: Not submitted [reproduced with Buildroot's reproducible date wrapper]
Signed-off-by: PhantoNull <65261018+PhantoNull@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 Configure | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/Configure
+++ b/Configure
@@ -3918,7 +3918,9 @@
 
 : who configured the system
-cf_time=`LC_ALL=C; LANGUAGE=C; export LC_ALL; export LANGUAGE; $date 2>&1`
+# Only stdout is a timestamp. A date wrapper's stderr diagnostics must not
+# become executable lines in the generated config.sh header.
+cf_time=`LC_ALL=C; LANGUAGE=C; export LC_ALL; export LANGUAGE; $date`
 case "$cf_by" in
 "")
 	cf_by=`(logname) 2>/dev/null`
 	case "$cf_by" in
